# AI Policy

Version: 0.1, week-1 draft. Owner: [TODO: your name].
Scope: this repository, including the Appium and API test suites. Applies to any AI agent, such as Claude Code, Cursor, or Codex, and to any human applying an AI-generated diff.

Ground rule: every line below must be backed by something observed in this repo, and every rule must name how its violation is detected. A rule whose violation cannot be detected is not a rule, it is a wish.

## Allowed changes

What the agent may generate or modify, and the proof required before the change is accepted.

| Allowed change | Condition: proof required | How a violation is detected |
|---|---|---|
| New tests, page objects, and actions under `appium-tests/src` | Output of a local OS-specific repository runner (`run-suite.ps1` or `run-suite.sh`) attached to the PR | Reviewer rejects missing, cached, red, or 0-test run output |
| New clients, models, test data, and tests under `api-tests/src` | `fake-api` is running and a fresh `:api-tests:test --rerun` result shows a non-zero test count with zero failures | Reviewer rejects missing, red, connection-failed, or 0-test run output |
